  "title": "alljoyn: Fix compilation on 32-bit platforms",
  "description": "On platforms where a pointer is 32-bit, e.g., armhf, comparing the\ndifference of two pointers to an unsigned integer is a sign-compare\nerror. Cast to avoid:\n\n\t/<<PKGBUILDDIR>>/epan/dissectors/packet-alljoyn.c: In function ‘parse_arg’:\n\t/<<PKGBUILDDIR>>/epan/dissectors/packet-alljoyn.c:1182:46: error: comparison of integer expressions of different signedness: ‘int’ and ‘unsigned int’ [-Werror=sign-compare]\n\t 1182 |             while(((sig_pointer - sig_saved) < (length - 1)) && (tvb_reported_length_remaining(tvb, offset) > 0)) {\n\t      |                                              ^\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
